#4471 was marked **known** with one fix queued. The data says that is one ticket for at least two
bugs, and five reports that may be a third. Each problem below has its own ticket in
[em-hache/what-it-shows](https://github.com/em-hache/what-it-shows/issues).

## The problems

| Problem | Reports | Ticket |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Day-first dates read month first (parser) | 379 | [#1](https://github.com/em-hache/what-it-shows/issues/1) |
| Booking-v3 hint shows MM/DD to day-first tenants | 33 | [#2](https://github.com/em-hache/what-it-shows/issues/2) |
| Not a month flip: one-day shifts, time zone, early invite | 5 | [#3](https://github.com/em-hache/what-it-shows/issues/3) |

The first two rows add up to 412, the number merged into #4471. The 5 reports in row three are
inside those 379, so the counts above overlap by 5.

<Callout kind="warn">
A fix for the parser does not fix the booking-v3 form. The form tells tenants to type MM/DD, so a
parser fix alone leaves 33 reports open.
</Callout>

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges a report by its subject line. All of
these reports use one of about a dozen subjects, such as "Wrong day on the invite", so they
merged into #4471 whatever their cause. Intake's tag is a guess: it tagged 15 of the 33 form
reports as `parser`.

## Next

- Fix the parser to read day-first locales day first (ticket 1).
- Change the booking-v3 hint for day-first tenants (ticket 2).
- Triage the 5 reports in ticket 3 before they are closed with the others.

